rzmq 0.5.26: io_uring multishot reader — survive the cancel CQE arriving before the
cancelled op's final -ECANCELED CQE.

When a RECV_MULTISHOT is cancelled, the kernel usually posts the ASYNC_CANCEL's own CQE
first and the cancelled op's terminal -ECANCELED CQE afterwards. MultishotReader forgot
the op on the first CQE, so the second one matched nothing, and the worker force-closed
the connection ("Handshake Safety Gate: multishot CQE not delegated"). Upstream only
cancels while closing, so it went unnoticed; any cancel on a live connection hit it. The
reader now waits for both CQEs, in either order. Adds MultishotReader::is_idle().

